<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Reference//EN" "reference.dtd">
<reference id="parameters" xml:lang="en-GB">
  <title>Build parameters</title>
  <shortdesc>Parameters are passed on the command line as
    <codeph>-Dname=value</codeph>, or in a DITA-OT project file.</shortdesc>
  <refbody>
    <section>
      <title>Plugin parameters</title>
      <table frame="all">
        <title>govuk.* parameters</title>
        <tgroup cols="3">
          <colspec colname="c1" colwidth="1.2*"/>
          <colspec colname="c2" colwidth="1*"/>
          <colspec colname="c3" colwidth="2*"/>
          <thead>
            <row>
              <entry>Parameter</entry>
              <entry>Values</entry>
              <entry>Purpose</entry>
            </row>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <entry><codeph>govuk.branding</codeph></entry>
              <entry><codeph>neutral</codeph> (default), <codeph>official</codeph></entry>
              <entry>Branding mode. Official mode is reserved for genuine GOV.UK services
                and is not yet implemented; see <xref keyref="branding"/>.</entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry><codeph>govuk.service.name</codeph></entry>
              <entry>text</entry>
              <entry>The name in the masthead and footer. Defaults to the map title, or a
                bookmap's main book title.</entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry><codeph>govuk.homepage.layout</codeph></entry>
              <entry><codeph>auto</codeph> (default), <codeph>start</codeph>,
                <codeph>annotated</codeph>, <codeph>list</codeph>, <codeph>grid</codeph>,
                <codeph>grouped</codeph>, <codeph>accordion</codeph></entry>
              <entry>Landing-page layout. <codeph>auto</codeph> chooses from the map's
                shape; see <xref keyref="navigation"/>.</entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry><codeph>govuk.search</codeph></entry>
              <entry><codeph>auto</codeph> (default), <codeph>yes</codeph>,
                <codeph>no</codeph></entry>
              <entry>Site search; see <xref keyref="search"/>.</entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry><codeph>govuk.pagefind.cmd</codeph></entry>
              <entry>path</entry>
              <entry>Location of the Pagefind executable when it is not on the
                <codeph>PATH</codeph>.</entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry namest="c1" nameend="c3">Further parameters — phase banner, footer
                links, favicon — arrive with their features; each is listed here when it
                lands.</entry>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
    </section>
    <section>
      <title>Inherited toolkit parameters</title>
      <p>Because <codeph>govuk</codeph> extends the toolkit's <codeph>html5</codeph>
        transformation, its standard parameters continue to work. The most useful:</p>
      <simpletable>
        <sthead>
          <stentry>Parameter</stentry>
          <stentry>Effect</stentry>
        </sthead>
        <strow>
          <stentry><codeph>args.css</codeph>, <codeph>args.cssroot</codeph>,
            <codeph>args.copycss</codeph></stentry>
          <stentry>Append your own stylesheet after the plugin's, for per-site tweaks.</stentry>
        </strow>
        <strow>
          <stentry><codeph>nav-toc</codeph></stentry>
          <stentry>Sidebar tree depth; the plugin defaults it to <codeph>full</codeph>.</stentry>
        </strow>
        <strow>
          <stentry><codeph>args.filter</codeph></stentry>
          <stentry>DITAVAL file for conditional builds.</stentry>
        </strow>
      </simpletable>
    </section>
  </refbody>
</reference>
